	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The primary analysis used “23 common baseline variables that were complete (with no missing data points) for all participants,” which is best classified as complete case analysis. Data preprocessing was described: variables were defined by type, attrition classes were encoded as 1/2/3, numeric and ordinal variables were rescaled between −1 and +1, and categorical variables were dummy coded. I found no mention of class-imbalance handling and no released code repository; only function names and package details were provided. Because a separate training/test split was not reported, training and test sample sizes are NR.

